1: <!--
2: 	ALE-386: one Intake on the workshop console — its state, minor badge,
3: 	medical flag, origin, live hold, refund, Carried Fee (ALE-388), the Intake Email log (scheduled
4: 	emails marked), its history and link generation — and the commands
5: 	Phoenix says are valid now (`availableCommands`; after finalisation,
6: 	ALE-393's corrections from `attendanceCorrections`). The UI never works out
7: 	Intake rules: it shows Phoenix's list, and the boundary decides again
8: 	under the lock, answering a stale command with its named reason. All
9: 	commands are submit buttons of one form, so the optional note goes with
10: 	whichever is pressed. There is no copy-link: a link is only ever resent
11: 	or rotated. (ALE-387) Withdraw needs the refund-or-forfeit choice and
12: 	(ALE-389) Refund credit a confirmation, so both are the refund module's
13: 	(ALE-421) in the workshop scope; a paid Intake shows the refund-timing
14: 	hint Phoenix works out (`refundTimingDaysToGo`) when the workshop is 7
15: 	days away or closer.
16: -->
17: <script lang="ts">
18: import type { BeginnersWorkshopRosterIntake } from "@dhc/api-client";
19: import { HeartPulse, Link2 } from "@lucide/svelte";
20: import { toast } from "svelte-sonner";
